        "name": "I-10 (Katy Freeway)",
        "designation": "I-10 West",
        "construction_year": 1960,
        "completion_year": 1968,
        "decade": "1960s",
        "neighborhoods_displaced": [
          "Fourth Ward"
        ],
        "description": "The Katy Freeway's construction devastated the historic Fourth Ward (Freedmenstown), one of Houston's oldest African American neighborhoods established by formerly enslaved people after the Civil War. The freeway's wide right-of-way demolished blocks of Victorian-era shotgun houses and displaced a community with deep cultural roots stretching back to Reconstruction."
