        "completion_year": 1962,
        "decade": "1960s",
        "neighborhoods_displaced": [
          "Third Ward",
          "Midtown"
        ],
        "description": "The Southwest Freeway tore through Midtown and the northern edge of the Third Ward, one of Houston's most historically significant African American neighborhoods and home to Texas Southern University. The freeway created a physical barrier that accelerated the decline of Black-owned businesses and severed the connection between the Third Ward and downtown Houston."
