      "properties": {
        "name": "I-610 (Inner Loop)",
        "designation": "I-610",
        "construction_year": 1955,
        "completion_year": 1970,
        "decade": "1960s",
        "neighborhoods_displaced": [
          "Independence Heights",
          "Eastwood"
        ],
        "description": "The I-610 Loop took fifteen years to complete and formed a roughly 38-mile ring around central Houston. Its northern segment demolished portions of Independence Heights, one of the first self-governing African American municipalities in Texas, incorporated in 1915. On the east side, the freeway bisected the Eastwood neighborhood, a diverse working-class community."
